-- title:
--   Descending equality of Deligne data from B[1/e][1/f] to B[1/c]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $K_0$ a field that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, $\pi \in \mathcal O$, and let $B$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra. Let $\mathfrak p \subset B$ be a prime ideal, let $e \in B$ with $e \notin \mathfrak p$, and let $f \in B[1/e] =$ `Localization.Away e` be an element not lying in the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak p$ under $B \to B[1/e]$. Let $P, P'$ be two points of the functor `Omega K₀ π` at $B$, that is, two Deligne data over $B$: families of $B$-submodules $\mathrm{line}\,M \subseteq B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$, indexed by the full $\mathcal O$-lattices $M$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotient, compatible with lattice inclusions and with homothety by $K_0^\times$, and satisfying the nondegeneracy condition at every prime of $B$ recorded in the structure. Assume that the images of $P$ and $P'$ in `Omega K₀ π` at $B[1/e][1/f] =$ `Localization.Away f`, obtained by pushing forward along the canonical $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $B \to B[1/e] \to B[1/e][1/f]$ (pushforward being the $B'$-span of the image of the submodules under base change), coincide. The conclusion is that there exists $c \in B$ with $c \notin \mathfrak p$ such that the images of $P$ and $P'$ in `Omega K₀ π` at `Localization.Away c` already coincide.
--
--   This is the localisation bookkeeping step allowing an equality of points of the formal upper half plane functor $\widehat\Omega$ over an iterated localisation to be realised over a single basic open neighbourhood of a given prime. It is used in the uniqueness-up-to-localisation argument for lifting families along square-zero extensions in the fine moduli discussion, [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero).
